<theodulf. carm. 74.1>	Primus amoena tenens factoris munere rura
<theodulf. carm. 74.2>	Helisii celsi tum bene factus homo,
<theodulf. carm. 74.3>	Floribus umbriferis vitam peragebat in arvis,
<theodulf. carm. 74.4>	Quo, paradise, tuus vernat amoenus ager.
<theodulf. carm. 74.5>	Florigeras sedes, iucundo et murmure rivos,
<theodulf. carm. 74.6>	Undique stipatos floribus atque rosis.
<theodulf. carm. 74.7>	Arborei foetus vario quo stipite pendent,
<theodulf. carm. 74.8>	Perpetuo numquam desit ademtus ei.
<theodulf. carm. 74.9>	Illic multigeni pariuntur cespite flores,
<theodulf. carm. 74.10>	Malorum fructus fertilis almus ager;
<theodulf. carm. 74.11>	Quo crepitans croceum pirum rubet arbore, foeta
<theodulf. carm. 74.12>	Ficus odorifico flore virescit ubi.
<theodulf. carm. 74.13>	Puniceo tellus flavescit cortice pomo,
<theodulf. carm. 74.14>	Et laurus redolet, mirtus opaca simul.
<theodulf. carm. 74.15>	Lenta liquore madens, geminis et turgida baccis
<theodulf. carm. 74.16>	Quove canis olea stat honerata suis.
<theodulf. carm. 74.17>	Arbor in inmensum spaciatur nomine vitae
<theodulf. carm. 74.18>	Helisii medio e vertice surgit eri.
<theodulf. carm. 74.19>	Mille soporatas profert pulcherrimus herbas
<theodulf. carm. 74.20>	Campus inauditas, quas dat amoenus ager.
